    "body": "### User Story\r\n\r\nAs a user, I would like Status to use uniform User-Agent HTTP headers on both platforms.\r\n\r\n### Description\r\n\r\n*Type*: Improvement\r\n\r\n*Summary*: Use Status-specific user-agent header, so identifying Status users is simpler\r\n\r\nCurrently, the following user-agent strings are used:\r\n\r\niOS: `StatusIm/1234 CFNetwork/808.3 Darwin/16.3.0`\r\nAndroid: `\"okhttp/3.4.1\"`\r\n\r\nThe immediate benefit of this will be getting metrics of Status users on commiteth.com.\r\n\r\n### Solution\r\nI propose `StatusIm <version>/<platform>` for the header value.\r\n\r\nThis blog post has instructions on how to set the header: http://blog.bigbinary.com/2016/07/10/passing-user-agent-or-custom-header-in-react-native-webview.html\r\n",
